A Private Network Interface is the network interface that connects an Instance to a
Private Network. An Instance can have multiple private network interfaces at the same
time, but each private network interface must belong to a different Private Network.

USAGE:
  scw instance private-network-interface <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create      Create a private network interface
  delete      Delete a private network interface
  get         Get a private network interface
  list        List private network interfaces
  update      Update a private network interface

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for private-network-interface
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource

Use "scw instance private-network-interface [command] --help" for more information about a command.
